      "rationale": "Highly relevant to localization/region-fit reasoning. Mostly plausible, but some values are inferred beyond the terse text (VC firms as 'on_site_required' is a reasonable domain inference rather than text-derived), acceptable but not strongly grounded."
    },
    {
      "name": "localization_dependency",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.95,
      "source_groundedness": 0.7,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "This is the exact axis the query needs to assess fit for a new region. Categorisations are generally warranted, though several rely on domain priors (VC=high_local_knowledge) not explicit in the one-line descriptions; still a sound inference."
    },
    {
      "name": "current_geographic_presence",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.75,
      "source_groundedness": 0.5,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "Useful for region-fit baseline, but the descriptions rarely state geographic footprint. Values like 'single_region_concentrated' vs 'global_presence' appear asserted without textual support; 23andMe/Addepar operate globally yet labeled single-region. Address gives location but not presence extent."
    },
    {
      "name": "customer_engagement_model",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.85,
      "source_groundedness": 0.75,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Adds a genuine axis (B2B vs consumer vs enterprise) relevant to a service/localization pivot. Values mostly track descriptions well (VC=enterprise_relationship_intensive, 23andMe=consumer_direct), with occasional inference."
    },
    {
      "name": "physical_infrastructure_intensity",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.85,
      "source_groundedness": 0.65,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "Relevant to localized-delivery feasibility. But several values are unsupported/contradictory: 23andMe labeled 'capital_intensive_physical' and 5AM Ventures 'capital_intensive_physical' are not warranted by their texts, while a VC firm elsewhere is 'software_only'—inconsistent and partly invented."
    }
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.9,
  "source_groundedness": 0.68,
  "rationale": "The added columns collectively give strong, non-redundant analytical leverage precisely aligned with the query about service/localization pivots and region fit: business model, localization dependency, delivery mode, engagement, and infrastructure are all genuine grouping/modeling axes. Groundedness is the weaker dimension: descriptions are single sentences, so several categorisations (especially geographic_presence and physical_infrastructure_intensity) rest on unsupported or even contradictory assertions rather than the source text. Business_model_category and customer_engagement_model are best grounded."
